# Cetana Labs — Sleek UI (SvelteKit) environment template (RFC-LAB-000-008 M1)
# Copy to .env for local dev. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed vars to the client
# bundle — required here because the app is a static SPA (ssr = false).

# --- PocketBase data source (BK-011 / M1) ---
# Base URL of the live PocketBase backend the data layer reads structural data from.
VITE_PB_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# Data source switch: `pocketbase` (live SDK), `snapshot` (bundled static/data/*.json),
# or unset/`auto` (PocketBase when reachable, snapshot fallback). Default: auto.
# VITE_PB_SOURCE=auto

# --- Auth (BK-011 / M2) ---
# GitHub OAuth needs NO frontend env var — the client id/secret are configured in the
# PocketBase admin on the `users` collection (v0.40+: Collections → users → Options →
# OAuth2 → GitHub). The SDK reads the provider config from PB via VITE_PB_URL above.
# Setup: docs/guides/developer-guide.md → GitHub OAuth setup.

# --- Production (BK-011 / M5, RFC-LAB-000-011: Vercel + Railway) ---
# In production the SPA is built on Vercel; set VITE_PB_URL there (Vercel project env)
# to the Railway PocketBase URL — do NOT hardcode it here:
#   VITE_PB_URL = https://<your-app>.up.railway.app
# No secret belongs in the frontend bundle; OAuth is configured on the Railway PB.
# Runbook: docs/guides/developer-guide.md → "Deployment".
